  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute low back strain (S39.012A)</content>. Mechanical low back pain after heavy lifting, with no red flags: no saddle numbness, weakness, fever, or cancer history, and the bladder empties fully, so cauda equina compression and urinary retention are excluded clinically. Imaging is not indicated. [S]<list><item>Heat, keep walking, and avoid heavy splitting for two weeks; bed rest is not advised.</item><item>Ibuprofen 400 mg three times a day with food for up to seven days, with acetaminophen as needed; kidney function is normal.</item><item>No skeletal muscle relaxant: they add sedation, and some have anticholinergic effects that can make it harder to empty the bladder; no opioid.</item><item>Return the same day for leg weakness, numbness in the groin, difficulty passing urine, or fever.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Delusional disorder, persecutory type, on aripiprazole (F22)</content>. Seven weeks into aripiprazole 5 mg without akathisia or sedation. Weight 64.0 kg, up 0.8 kg from baseline (1.3 percent); this serves as the eight-week weight check. [S]<list><item>Continue aripiprazole 5 mg each morning.</item><item>Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or of harming anyone; safety plan and the 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline confirmed.</item><item>Twelve-week review as booked.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: CMID: Clinical Monitoring Intelligence Database, depression, bipolar, and mood disorders monograph (PHQ-9, suicide-risk review, and second-generation antipsychotic monitoring) (2026); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); Noninvasive Treatments for Acute, Subacute, and Chronic Low Back Pain: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians. Ann Intern Med 2017;166(7):514-530 (2017)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Telephone check in one week; twelve-week review as booked. Next scheduled visit 2026-07-14: twelve-week aripiprazole and urethroplasty follow-up. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
